    "created_at": "2024-02-26T08:00:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-26T08:00:35Z",
    "body": "I have a work in progress Chromium CL. [This version](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/5232387/12) is passing all the tests but is ugly bad code; [this version](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/5232387) is my attempt at refactoring but it's now failing some of the tests, so we shouldn't trust it yet. But, it can give you an idea of what I expect the changes to look like:\r\n\r\n- More first-class tracking of close watcher groups, instead of using \"is grouped with previous\" / \"created with user activation\".\r\n- Tracking the amount of allowed groups, in a way that increments / decrements at appropriate points in time.\r\n- Using those to figure out (a) when creating a new close watcher, whether it goes into the topmost existing group or a new group; (b) whether we can fire the cancel event.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
